WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.829
Hi, I'm Pecan!

00:00:02.829 --> 00:00:08.053
OpenMuse is a self-hostable personal agent that says it works with any agent harness.

00:00:08.053 --> 00:00:10.292
Here's how, and what stays behind.

00:00:11.558 --> 00:00:12.984
OpenMuse doesn't integrate harnesses.

00:00:12.984 --> 00:00:17.262
It speaks one protocol, and any agent that speaks it too drops

00:00:17.262 --> 00:00:18.688
into a single slot.

00:00:21.758 --> 00:00:24.243
The app talks to a small server.

00:00:24.243 --> 00:00:26.727
One environment variable decides which agent answers.

00:00:27.147 --> 00:00:31.635
By default, a built-in agent answers, and it brings twenty-nine tools:

00:00:31.635 --> 00:00:33.267
mail, browser, terminal, files.

00:00:33.687 --> 00:00:37.469
Switch it to AG-UI, and any harness can answer instead: one request

00:00:37.469 --> 00:00:39.991
in, and a stream of typed events back.

00:00:40.411 --> 00:00:44.026
But the tools live inside the agent it replaced, and the app

00:00:44.026 --> 00:00:46.134
draws eight cards by exact tool name.

00:00:46.134 --> 00:00:49.147
A swapped-in harness gets a chat pane, and no cards.

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:53.014
The portability is real, and it's five lines.

00:00:53.014 --> 00:00:57.289
The one harness adapter in the tree is disabled, and connected to nothing.

00:00:59.942 --> 00:01:01.847
The agent's strongest tools only prepare.

00:01:01.847 --> 00:01:06.293
A prepared email waits for approval, and there is no tool to approve it.

00:01:06.713 --> 00:01:10.169
The proposal is hashed over its input, connection and target.

00:01:10.169 --> 00:01:14.316
Approving means presenting that hash from the app, so approval binds to

00:01:14.316 --> 00:01:15.698
exactly what you saw.

00:01:16.118 --> 00:01:20.800
One database update re-checks status, expiry and task state, so of two

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.750
racing approvals, exactly one wins.

00:01:24.308 --> 00:01:26.208
You can replace who does the talking.

00:01:26.208 --> 00:01:28.107
You cannot replace who holds the keys.

00:01:31.025 --> 00:01:32.783
To recap: the talking is swappable.

00:01:32.783 --> 00:01:35.714
The tools, the cards and the approval gate are not.

00:01:36.134 --> 00:01:38.200
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:38.790
I'm Pecan.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:39.085
Bye!
